33,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we're spending about 2,300 yen a month on supplies, often buying duplicates. Also, the management office charges 4,200 yen an hour for a cleaner, billed to one person.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A full pass takes about 102 minutes total. As for an outside firm, they have a two-hour arrival window and won't clean surfaces that aren't already tidied.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The calendar shows frequent absences, with some of us away for weeks. Also, kitchen use is heavily skewed; most of the mess comes from just a few of us.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"The bathroom grout gets dirty again in just eleven days, and it's clear we all have very different definitions of what ""done"" actually means for a room.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The house chat shows our arguments usually start with reminders about missed chores, and the previous tenants warned that permanent room assignments eventually ruined their friendship.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, if a full pass is nearly two hours, that's a significant chunk of time. Does the management office's hourly rate seem viable if we want to avoid that burden?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"It's a lot of time, but the outside firm's arrival window and the requirement to tidy first make it less convenient than it sounds. I'm not sure if the cost outweighs the effort.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Given the uneven kitchen use and the frequent absences I found, a rigid rotation might feel unfair to those who aren't here or don't contribute to the mess.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, I agree. If we don't have a shared standard of ""done,"" a rotation just means the quality of the house fluctuates wildly every week. We need something more consistent.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that if we focus too much on the ""fairness"" of who does what, we'll just end up arguing more. We need a solution that doesn't lead to the same friction the previous tenants had.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we go with a professional service, we can eliminate the disputes over standards and timing, though we'll need a clear way to handle the monthly billing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm still concerned about the ""tidying first"" requirement. If we have to do the hard work of clearing surfaces anyway, are we actually saving that much time?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. If we're still managing the clutter and the schedule, we're just paying for someone to do the final wipe-down. We need a system that accounts for actual usage.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"But if we don't have a professional standard, we're just cycling through different levels of cleanliness. I can't stand the guesswork of whether the kitchen is actually clean or just ""May-clean.""","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Maybe we can find a middle ground that doesn't feel like a chore or a source of conflict. If we avoid permanent assignments, we might avoid the bitterness the previous tenants felt.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"We should consider the financial aspect carefully. If we pay for a service, we must ensure the billing is transparent so no one is left out of pocket.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm leaning away from the outside firm if it doesn't actually remove the time burden. I'd rather we find a way to manage the hours ourselves without it feeling like a second job.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I think we need to weigh the cost of a service against the frustration of an unfair rota. If we can't agree on a standard, maybe paying for consistency is the only way to keep the peace.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I agree with Benjamin. If we can't agree on what ""clean"" means, we'll just keep fighting. Paying for a professional standard seems like the only way to stop the guessing game.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I just want us to be happy. If paying for a service prevents the reminders and rows that Midori saw in the chat, it might be worth the cost for our friendship.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
